const e={readingNotes:[{title:{zh:"研究问题",en:"Research question"},body:{zh:"论文提出保留时间序列依赖结构的 stationary bootstrap 重采样方法。 阅读时先把它理解为一个被界定的问题，而不是可以脱离样本、时间和制度环境的结论。",en:"“The Stationary Bootstrap” frames a bounded research question. Read the stated question together with the named sample, dates, and institutional setting rather than treating it as a conclusion that automatically travels to another market or period."},reference:{url:"https://doi.org/10.1080/01621459.1994.10476870",label:{zh:"Journal of the American Statistical Association (1994) · 来源说明",en:"Journal of the American Statistical Association (1994) · source description"}}},{title:{zh:"研究设计",en:"Research design"},body:{zh:"方法通过随机区块长度和连续观测片段构造重采样序列，设计选择决定其保留的依赖特征。 这说明比较对象、观察窗口和对照关系是研究合同的一部分；改变其中任何一项，都可能改变所检验的命题。",en:"For “The Stationary Bootstrap”, the source describes a deliberate comparison, observation window, and control relation. Those choices are part of its research contract: changing one can change the proposition being tested, even when the method label remains the same."},reference:{url:"https://doi.org/10.1080/01621459.1994.10476870",label:{zh:"Journal of the American Statistical Association (1994) · 来源说明",en:"Journal of the American Statistical Association (1994) · source description"}}},{title:{zh:"数据与时点",en:"Data and timing"},body:{zh:"输入是按固定时钟排序的完整时间序列、缺失处理规则、抽样区块设置和统计量定义。 数据字段、可得时点和样本筛选需要与原始研究分开记录，不能仅凭同名变量或最终修订数据就视为可比。",en:"For “The Stationary Bootstrap”, keep the fields, their availability timing, and the sample filters separate from the original study. A same-named variable, later-revised database, or matching end-of-period date is not automatically a comparable input."},reference:{url:"https://doi.org/10.1080/01621459.1994.10476870",label:{zh:"Journal of the American Statistical Association (1994) · 来源说明",en:"Journal of the American Statistical Association (1994) · source description"}}},{title:{zh:"如何理解结果",en:"How to read the result"},body:{zh:"它提供对时间依赖数据进行不确定性评估的一种工具，而不是使任何小样本或非平稳数据自动可靠。 它支持的是该来源所描述的经验或理论关系；它本身不把相关性、模型拟合或历史表现升级为因果、可执行性或未来保证。",en:"For “The Stationary Bootstrap”, the source supports only the empirical or theoretical relation it describes. It does not turn association, model fit, or historical performance into causality, a directly executable procedure, or a guarantee about subsequent outcomes."},reference:{url:"https://doi.org/10.1080/01621459.1994.10476870",label:{zh:"Journal of the American Statistical Association (1994) · 来源说明",en:"Journal of the American Statistical Association (1994) · source description"}}},{title:{zh:"复核清单",en:"Replication checks"},body:{zh:"记录频率、缺失段和区块长度设定，检验重采样是否尊重交易时段和结构断点，并保存随机种子。 在做后续分析前，应把这些选择写入版本化的研究记录，并保留原始来源链接与访问日期。",en:"Before extending “The Stationary Bootstrap”, record its sample, timing, construction choices, and source edition in a versioned note. Keep the primary-source link and access date so a later reader can distinguish a changed definition from a changed result."},reference:{url:"https://doi.org/10.1080/01621459.1994.10476870",label:{zh:"Journal of the American Statistical Association (1994) · 来源说明",en:"Journal of the American Statistical Association (1994) · source description"}}},{title:{zh:"适用边界",en:"Scope boundary"},body:{zh:"该条导读引用 Journal of the American Statistical Association (1994)。重采样假设无法替代对非平稳、制度变化或样本选择的诊断，更不证明预测或策略有效。 若需要量化结论、参数、表格或稳健性检验，请回到原文并单独核对版本、附录与样本定义。",en:"This guide cites Journal of the American Statistical Association (1994) for “The Stationary Bootstrap”. Its public description defines the boundary. For numerical conclusions, parameters, tables, or robustness tests, return to the original and separately verify the edition, appendices, and sample definitions."},reference:{url:"https://doi.org/10.1080/01621459.1994.10476870",label:{zh:"Journal of the American Statistical Association (1994) · 来源说明",en:"Journal of the American Statistical Association (1994) · source description"}}}],readerLimits:{zh:"本文只整理“The Stationary Bootstrap”所公开说明的研究问题与设计边界，不构成收益预测、交易规则或全文复现。重采样假设无法替代对非平稳、制度变化或样本选择的诊断，更不证明预测或策略有效。",en:"This guide only organizes the publicly described question and design of “The Stationary Bootstrap”. It is not a return forecast, trading rule, or full-text replication. The source's stated scope remains controlling."}};export{e as default};
